/**

@brief Tests
@defgroup all_tests Tests
@details
A test is code that checks a piece of software behaves as specified. Each test case
makes a claim about one behaviour (a return value, a state change, a rejected input)
and fails if the claim does not hold. Tests catch regressions and document the
expected behaviour of the code they cover.

In Zephyr, tests are built on the Ztest framework. A test file defines one or more
suites with ZTEST_SUITE(), and each test case is written with the
<a href="https://docs.zephyrproject.org/latest/doxygen/html/group__ztest__test.html#gac25858f76ea667d07de422a3b489cb15">ZTEST()</a>
macro, which uses assertions such as zassert_equal() to check its results.
Optional setup and teardown functions run before and after the cases in a suite.

Each test directory is a small Zephyr application. A testcase.yaml declares the test
identifiers, their tags, and the platforms they may run on. Twister, Zephyr's test runner, walks the
test roots, reads these files, builds each selected test for its platform, and runs it.

Test areas are grouped by subsystem, and each area below has its own page. The platform
list on each page is the set twister selects for that area's testcase.yaml files, so it
follows the configuration rather than being written by hand.

Upstream documentation:

- [Testing overview](https://docs.zephyrproject.org/latest/develop/test/index.html)
- [Twister test runner](https://docs.zephyrproject.org/latest/develop/test/twister.html)
- [Test configuration in Twister](https://docs.zephyrproject.org/latest/develop/test/twister.html#twister_tests_long_version)
- [Harnesses](https://docs.zephyrproject.org/latest/develop/test/twister.html#twister_harnesses)
- [Ztest test framework](https://docs.zephyrproject.org/latest/develop/test/ztest.html#test-framework)
- [Ztest unit testing quick start](https://docs.zephyrproject.org/latest/develop/test/ztest.html#ztest_unit_testing)

@{
@}

*/
